{
  "project": "xschema",
  "description": "Centralized Unsupported Keyword Detection - Move keyword detection from TS to Go CLI with context-aware unevaluated support",
  "userStories": [
    {
      "id": "US-001",
      "title": "Establish compliance baseline",
      "description": "As a maintainer, I need to capture current compliance state before changes to detect regressions.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Run `bun run compliance` on zod adapter, note passed/failed/unsupported counts",
        "Run `bun run compliance` on arktype adapter, note passed/failed/unsupported counts",
        "Run `bun run compliance` on valibot adapter, note passed/failed/unsupported counts",
        "Run `bun run compliance` on effect adapter, note passed/failed/unsupported counts",
        "Record baseline in notes field for regression comparison"
      ],
      "passes": true,
      "notes": "Baseline captured 2026-01-13: zod(4299p/0f/73u), arktype(4299p/0f/73u), valibot(4249p/50f/73u), effect(4299p/0f/73u). Unsupported=73 (33 dynamicRef + 40 recursiveRef). Valibot has 10 failures per draft except draft3."
    },
    {
      "id": "US-002",
      "title": "Define UnsupportedKeywordError type",
      "description": "As a developer, I need a typed error for unsupported keywords so callers can distinguish it from other errors.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Add `UnsupportedKeywordError` struct in `cli/unsupported/unsupported.go` after line 22",
        "Struct has fields: Keyword string, Reason string, Path string",
        "Implements `error` interface with Error() method returning descriptive message",
        "Update `ValidateKeywords()` return type to `*UnsupportedKeywordError` (not generic error)",
        "`go vet ./unsupported/` passes",
        "`go test ./unsupported/` passes"
      ],
      "passes": false,
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "US-003",
      "title": "Add context-aware unevaluated detection",
      "description": "As a user, I want unevaluatedProperties to work standalone but error when combined with applicators.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Replace `validateNode()` and `validateObject()` in unsupported.go (lines 101-132) with context-aware implementation",
        "Add `hasPropertyApplicators()` helper checking: allOf, anyOf, oneOf, if, $ref, dependentSchemas, not",
        "Add `hasItemApplicators()` helper checking: prefixItems, contains, allOf, anyOf, oneOf, if",
        "`unevaluatedProperties` standalone returns nil (allowed)",
        "`unevaluatedProperties` with any property applicator returns UnsupportedKeywordError",
        "`unevaluatedItems` standalone returns nil (allowed)",
        "`unevaluatedItems` with any item applicator returns UnsupportedKeywordError",
        "Detection recurses into nested schemas",
        "`go test ./unsupported/` passes"
      ],
      "passes": false,
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "US-004",
      "title": "Unit tests for keyword detection",
      "description": "As a developer, I need comprehensive tests for the keyword detection logic.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Test: $dynamicRef detected at root returns error",
        "Test: $dynamicRef nested in properties returns error",
        "Test: unevaluatedProperties standalone returns nil",
        "Test: unevaluatedProperties + allOf returns error",
        "Test: unevaluatedProperties + $ref returns error",
        "Test: unevaluatedItems standalone returns nil",
        "Test: unevaluatedItems + prefixItems returns error",
        "Test: fully supported schema returns nil",
        "`go test ./unsupported/ -v` passes"
      ],
      "passes": false,
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "US-005",
      "title": "Integrate validation into processor",
      "description": "As a user running xschema generate, I want early errors when my schema contains unsupported keywords.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Add import `github.com/xschemadev/xschema/unsupported` to cli/processor/processor.go",
        "In bundleAll() after vocabulary filtering (~line 263), call unsupported.ValidateKeywords()",
        "Unmarshal bundled schema to map[string]any before calling ValidateKeywords",
        "If ValidateKeywords returns error, wrap with source URI and return",
        "Existing processor tests still pass",
        "`go test ./processor/` passes"
      ],
      "passes": false,
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "US-006",
      "title": "Compliance catches UnsupportedKeywordError and skips",
      "description": "As a compliance runner, I want tests with unsupported keywords automatically skipped not failed.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Add `unsupportedErr *unsupported.UnsupportedKeywordError` field to bundledGroup struct (line ~363)",
        "In bundleSchemas() error handling, use errors.As to check for UnsupportedKeywordError",
        "When UnsupportedKeywordError caught, set bundledGroup.unsupportedErr instead of bundleErr",
        "Update markBundleErrors() to handle unsupportedErr separately from bundleErr",
        "For unsupportedErr: add all tests in group to summary.UnsupportedFeatures",
        "For bundleErr: call markAllFailed as before",
        "`go test ./compliance/` passes"
